<title>AUSTRIA: Daimler sees profit push from Gemini sale.</title>
<headline>Daimler sees profit push from Gemini sale.</headline>
<dateline>SALZBURG, Austria 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz unit Debis said on Thursday the sale of its Cap Gemini stake to Gemini would have a big impact on 1997 earnings which would also give a strong push to current-year group earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;This will have a very big impact on our earnings, and of course on the group's earnings as well,&quot; a Debis spokesman told Reuters during a meeting of eastern European business and political leaders in this Alpine city.</p>
<p>He declined to be more specific.</p>
<p>Debis earlier said Cap Gemini would pay 1.4 billion marks in cash for the 24.4 percent stake.</p>
<p>The services company also said it would cancel a recently launched convertible bond issue for the shares, repaying buyers of the notes four percent of their original investment.</p>
<p>-- Salzburg newsroom +43-662 879 976</p>
</text>
